.TH HTTP_FREE 3
.SH NAME
http_free \- release the memory of an HTTP client structure
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "void http_free(http* " h ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_free ()
frees the input and output buffers, all requests and responses (with their headers, bodies
and data) and the host name of
.IR h .
It does not close the connection, call
.BR http_close (3)
first. Afterwards the structure can be started again with
.BR http_init (3).
.SH NOTES
Without it every request of a long running program keeps about 48 kilobytes of buffers.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_close(3), http_init(3)
